      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "Boom colt LOUCASSO (7) backs up after stretching his perfect record here to five by coming from a wider barrier for a brilliant win in the Breeders Challenge 3CG Final last week. Up in distance but won last season's Breeders Crown Final over 2240m at Melton. Hard to tip against him. I AM THE STORM (11) has had seven weeks off since a brave placing in the Vicbred Final at Melton. Had won six of his previous seven and while the outside barrier makes his task tougher he hails from the yard of premier Victorian trainer Emma Stewart. Her horses must always be respected when they head north. ENJABONARLO (1) was 14m behind LOUCASSO last week but did come from a very wide barrier. Better served by the ace draw and won here three back. BUZZ BOMB (8) is worth including having continued his consistent form by coming from a similar draw to be beaten 3.7m last week.",
